    <item>
      <title>The Collapse of Non-Monetary Value Systems in the Modern West</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/posts/essays/the-collapse-of-non-monetary-value-systems/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 22 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/essays/the-collapse-of-non-monetary-value-systems/</guid>
      <description>Money was only a token of trust; when trust erodes, tokens lose meaning. The Stoics taught that wealth is indifferent, virtue essential. Rome collapsed not for lack of currency but for loss of civic virtue — citizens ceased to see the republic as an extension of themselves. The analogy is uncomfortably close. When Australians treat their country as a property portfolio rather than a common inheritance, they re-enact the same decline.</description>
